```

| The showcase, same sources | WebView | Native |
|---|---|---|
| App process | 70.2 MB | 30.4 MB |
| WebView renderer | 71.3 MB | none |
| **Total** | **141.5 MB** | **30.4 MB** |
| Release APK, arm64, CPU only | 10.4 MB | 12.4 MB |

The native build costs about 2 MB of APK: QuickJS, Yoga and the renderer's JavaScript. Speed where it matters is the same: the showcase's chat streams Llama 3.2 1B at 43 tokens/s on the CPU, against 40 with the WebView.

# Compared with Tauri and React Native

| | Oriel native | Oriel WebView | Tauri 2 | React Native |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| UI drawn by | Native views | System WebView | System WebView | Native views |
| UI written in | HTML, CSS, JS (a subset) | Any web stack | Any web stack | React Native components |
| JavaScript in | QuickJS (app) | V8 (renderer) | V8 (renderer) | Hermes (app) |
| Native side | Zig | Zig | Rust | Kotlin, C++ |
| Processes | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 |
| Memory, hello world | **20.3 MB** | 105.5 MB | 119.0 MB | 39.9 MB |
| Memory, the showcase | **30.4 MB** | 141.5 MB | — | — |
| APK, hello world | 3.1 MB | **0.85 MB** | 6.0 MB | 18.5 MB |
| Reuses a web app | Mostly | Yes | Yes | No |
| Desktop | Linux, Windows, macOS | Linux, Windows, macOS | Linux, Windows, macOS | Windows, macOS (separate projects) |
| Status | Experimental | Stable | Stable | Stable |

On Android. Memory is the total PSS of the app's processes on Android 15 (ChromeOS ARC), from `dumpsys meminfo`; APK sizes are release builds for arm64; React Native is 0.87. "Mostly": what the CSS above covers. The hello worlds: Oriel's is a line of text and a button; Tauri's and React Native's are their starter templates.

What the numbers say:

- **Without a browser, Oriel uses half of React Native's memory**, while keeping web code: 20.3 MB for a hello world against 39.9 MB, and the whole showcase (30.4 MB) uses less than React Native's hello world.
- **The WebView renderer is the smallest download** (0.85 MB): it uses the browser the system already has. The native renderer adds about 2 MB: QuickJS, Yoga and the renderer's JavaScript. React Native ships its engine and framework (18.5 MB).
- **The trade:** the WebView runs any web code; the native renderer runs the part of the web an app's interface uses, on Linux, Windows, macOS, iOS and Android.

# Three architectures

The same app can be drawn three ways. Oriel's WebView and its native renderer run the same HTML, CSS and JavaScript; React Native runs React components instead.

